VERDICT: FAIL. Independently found, real-data-reproduced defect (the
MajorExpenseTrends change_percent/direction sign inversion on a negative
previous, item 2 above) is distinct from checker-tests' criterion-3 finding
(missing regression tests on 2 mutated sites) and is a live correctness bug,
not a coverage gap: the tool emits an internally self-contradictory
CategoryTrend row (positive change_amount, negative change_percent, "down"
direction) on the household's actual ledger data one month after a
refund-dominant period, in the exact function CB3-D modified, which the
spec's own written downstream-trace requirement obligated the worker to
catch. Recommend the fix mirror CB3-E's own precedent: divide by
math.Abs(previous) in MajorExpenseTrends' changePercent calculation (and
guard the previous==0/current<0 case's direction label), then add a
committed regression test with previous<0 pinning both change_percent and
direction, extending the oracle to match (both ends re-validated per the
oracle-calibration rule).
